From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: eggdogo <eggdogo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 16:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] sweet: disable kmem claim shuffling and readjusting on 39-bit VA space

On SWEET (Cortex-A53 / MSM8916), the kernel address space is 39 bits
(112 GB total, of which 64 GB is reserved below LOW_GLOBAL_BASE_ADDRESS,
leaving only ~48 GB for kernel_map heap and submaps).
The total size of all registered claims (zones 8GB, compressor 8GB,
kmem_ptr_range 7.8GB, kmem_data_range 22GB, and fixed submaps) fills ~47 GB,
leaving less than 1 GB of margin.

When kmem_shuffle_claims() shuffles claims into a random order, if 'zones'
is shuffled late, its start address exceeds zone_restricted_va_max()
(32GB from KERNEL_PMAP_HEAP_RANGE_START due to C_SLOT_PACKED_PTR).
This triggers kmem_readjust_ranges(), which shifts claims by 8 GB to the
right without resetting the linear 'start' search offset, causing subsequent
large claims (such as kmem_ptr_range) to exceed VM_MAX_KERNEL_ADDRESS and
panic with:
  'kmem_range_init: vm_map_locate_space failing for claim kmem_ptr_range'

Disable kmem_shuffle_claims() and kmem_readjust_ranges() on SWEET so that
claims are allocated deterministically in their natural registration order,
where 'zones' is placed at ~0xfffffff011800000 (well within its 32GB bound)
and all submaps fit cleanly without overflow.
---
 osfmk/vm/vm_kern.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/osfmk/vm/vm_kern.c b/osfmk/vm/vm_kern.c
index 54edb01..866a2ce 100644
--- a/osfmk/vm/vm_kern.c
+++ b/osfmk/vm/vm_kern.c
@@ -3630,7 +3630,9 @@ kmem_scramble_ranges(void)
 	 * Shuffle registered claims
 	 */
 	assert(kmem_claim_count < UINT16_MAX);
+#if !defined(SWEET)
 	kmem_shuffle_claims();
+#endif
 
 	/*
 	 * Apply restrictions and determine range for each claim
@@ -3650,7 +3652,9 @@ kmem_scramble_ranges(void)
 		 * Re-adjust ranges if restriction not met
 		 */
 		if (sp_range->min_address && start > sp_range->min_address) {
+#if !defined(SWEET)
 			kmem_readjust_ranges(i);
+#endif
 		} else {
 			sp_range->min_address = start;
 			sp_range->max_address = end;
-- 
2.39.5
